facts:
Translations, reflections and rotations do not change side lengths or angles, so the image is always congruent to the original.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw (-5.0,-0.5) -- (-3.6,-0.5) -- (-4.85,0.85) -- cycle;
\draw (-4.0,0.9) -- (-2.6,0.9) -- (-3.85,2.25) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed, -{Stealth}] (-3.6,-0.5) -- (-2.6,0.9);
\node at (-3.8,-1.5) {Translation};
\draw (-1.9,-0.4) -- (-0.5,-0.4) -- (-1.75,0.95) -- cycle;
\draw (1.9,-0.4) -- (0.5,-0.4) -- (1.75,0.95) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,-0.9) -- (0,1.6);
\node at (0,-1.5) {Reflection};
\draw (2.9,-0.4) -- (4.3,-0.4) -- (3.05,0.95) -- cycle;
\draw (4.3,1.0) -- (4.3,-0.4) -- (5.65,0.85) -- cycle;
\fill (4.3,-0.4) circle (2.2pt);
\node at (4.2,-1.5) {Rotation};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Figures with the same shape but a different size are **not** congruent.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-5.2,-0.3) -- (-3.9,-0.3) -- (-4.6,0.85) -- cycle;
\draw (-3.4,-0.3) -- (-2.1,-0.3) -- (-2.8,0.85) -- cycle;
\node[align=center] at (-3.65,-1.3) {Same shape and size:\\ congruent};
\draw (0.2,-0.3) -- (1.5,-0.3) -- (0.8,0.85) -- cycle;
\draw (2.2,-0.3) -- (4.28,-0.3) -- (3.16,1.54) -- cycle;
\node[align=center] at (2.24,-1.3) {Same shape, different size:\\ not congruent};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

